Design Parameters
o Diameter/Disk Loading
o Large diameter/Low Disk Loading: Reduces power required
o Small diameter/High Disk Loading: Lower weight; smaller
problems with helicopter c. g. position; better ground clearance; better clearance with main rotor, horizontal stabilizer and tail boom.
o Aim for smallest possible diameter that meets all design
requirements.
o Tip speed
o Low tip speed : minimizes noise and compressibility effects.
Requires higher torque.
o High tip speed: minimizes component weight and stall effects. Higher noise, higher control forces.


Design Parameters
o Number of blades
o Fewer blades: cheaper to build and maintain
stubby blades & higher tip losses
o Thumb rules:
o Blade aspect ratio between 5 and 9.
o Solidity between 0.03 and 0.06.
o Twist
o Similar to main rotor blade.
o High twist is good for hover, but penalizes forward flight
performance.
o < 10 degrees twist is used.


